<title>ITALY: Eni hopes 1996 results up on '95 -chairman.</title>
<headline>Eni hopes 1996 results up on '95 -chairman.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian energy group Eni expects strong results for 1996 which might surpass record profits seen in 1995, chairman Guglielmo Moscato told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;We think things have gone very well,&quot; Moscato said. &quot;We are closing the (1996) accounts and it seems they might be even better than those of the year before,&quot; Moscato said.</p>
<p>Eni posted a net profit of 4.327 trillion lire in 1995. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
